From cf39e8f5665c45e064f1772375ae48dcc9eeb36b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 08:37:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(expenses): allow tagging a vendor (Business Partner) on
 regular expenses

Previously only Recurring Expenses could tag a vendor sub-ledger.
One-off Expenses had no way to link a Business Partner at all, so
their posted journal line never carried a Sub Ledger tag.

- createExpenseSchema: add optional business_partner_id (same
  Business Partners VENDOR list used elsewhere), keep vendor_name
  as a separate free-text payee field for one-offs that don't
  warrant a ledger card.
- expenses.service.ts: resolve business_partner_id to the internal
  Vendor bridge row via ensureVendorFromBusinessPartner (same
  pattern as RecurringExpense) in both createExpense and
  updateExpense; pass it through to postExpense so the expense
  line posts with the vendor tag. Also thread it through the
  recurring-approval "no open provision" branch, and include
  business_partner_id on the vendor include in listExpenses so the
  frontend can pre-select it on edit.
- journal.service.ts: postExpense takes an optional businessPartnerId
  and tags it onto the expense line.
- ExpenseListPage.tsx: add a Vendor select (from Business Partners,
  category VENDOR) above the free-text Payee field, wired into the
  create/edit form.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
